      "text": "[3:04PM] #Okota_Isolo  #TrafficUpdate \n\nVehicular movement on the Cele-Ijesha Link Bridge is fast and uninterrupted. The stretch from Cele through the Rain Oil/Ago Intersection to Ago Palace records free-flowing traffic. However, the return journey experiences slow-moving traffic.\n\nTravel along the Daleko–Mushin Bridge is smooth, with similar fast-moving conditions reported from 5 Star connecting to the Iyana Isolo underbridge. The Ilasa to Ijesha corridor, heading toward Mile 2, also remains free of congestion.\n\nThe Oke-Afa Bridge towards Pako records fast traffic in both directions. Similarly, the Pako, Akiti, Chemist, Ago Roundabout corridor is moving smoothly in both directions.\n\nTraffic on the Ilasa–Transformer stretch through Apata Junction is also fast in both directions. The Ibeh Road to Ago Roundabout route is free of delays in either direction.\n\nThe entire stretch from Kogberegbe through Ire-Akari, Ile Ibadan, Mustapha, Ishaga, College Road, Omonije, Aiye, Limca, and LASUTECH Roundabout reports smooth and uninterrupted movement in both directions.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
